# Tutorial 02 — Narration and Pacing
# textspeed, autodelay, wait, and line length — the tools that control how your scene breathes.

@scenario {{SCENARIO_PREFIX}}_tutorial_02_narration
@include {{CHARACTERS_INCLUDE}}
{{BG_DECL}}@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[set ui.textBoxAsset none]
[set ui.continueIndicator spinning_arrow]
[if tutorial_still]
[set ui.reduceMotion true]
[else]
[set ui.reduceMotion false]
[endif]
[if !tutorial_initialized]
[set tutorial_count 0]
[flag tutorial_initialized]
[endif]
[set ui.characterHeightFactor 1.5]
[set ui.characterBaselineY 1.5]
[set character.lavender.imageEffect none]
{{BG_START}}
[textspeed 28]
[autodelay 1650]
[show lavender center talking]
[wait 200]
Lavender: Read this line. It's arriving at textspeed 28 — the default. Now watch:
[textspeed 45]
Lavender: This line is textspeed 45. Each letter takes longer. The pace changes.
[textspeed 28]
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: That's the core of this lesson — three commands that control rhythm.

@label lesson_menu
[show lavender far_left talking]
> [textspeed] — character reveal speed -> section_textspeed
> [autodelay] — pause between lines -> section_autodelay
> [wait] — hard pauses -> section_waits
> Line length as a pacing tool -> section_line_length
